      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T01:10:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we just need to add segments as an additional thing to check for.\n\nI suspect changing it this way will cause Policies that actually cover multiple LEDs to fail.",
      "revId": "d7ffe330ade358fe61103dc9069c0c1cfba1c7ca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c604c36_39bf8163",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1548775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T01:19:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hypothetically if someone made a typo like this the script would give a false positive:\n```\npower-state-high-left {\n\tcharge-state \u003d \"LED_PWRS_CHARGE\";\n\t/* Battery percent range 99..100 */\n\tbatt-lvl \u003d \u003c99 100\u003e;\n\n\tcharge-port \u003d \u003c0\u003e; /* Left port */\n\n\tright-led {\n\t\tled-id \u003d \"EC_LED_ID_RIGHT_LED\";\n\n\t\t/* Turn off the right LED */\n\t\tcolor-0 {\n\t\t\tled-color \u003d \u003c\u0026right_led_off\u003e;\n\t\t};\n\t};\n\n\tleft-led {\n\t\tled-id \u003d \"EC_LED_ID_RIGHT_LED\";   \u003c\u003c should be left\n\t\t/* Left LED to White */\n\t\tcolor-1 {\n\t\t\tled-color \u003d \u003c\u0026left_led_white\u003e;\n\t\t};\n\t};\n};\n```",
      "parentUuid": "0e8b14d2_0176be36",
      "revId": "d7ffe330ade358fe61103dc9069c0c1cfba1c7ca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4228c774_4df161be",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1548775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T01:26:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or alternatively, just add `if led_id \u003d\u003d \"EC_LED_ID_LIGHTBAR_LED\"` in front of the break if we\u0027re not too worried about validating the specific functions of the lightbar.",
      "parentUuid": "7c604c36_39bf8163",
      "revId": "d7ffe330ade358fe61103dc9069c0c1cfba1c7ca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "535a1e74_9e6b47d6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T02:02:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In your example, a BUILD_ASSERT would fail because the led-id didn\u0027t match the color node. This mistake is difficult to make as it would require multiple inconsistent changes.\n\nMy point is that the original intent of the script (b/303489645) was to ensure a 1:1 correspondence between policy nodes and system states **for each LED ID**, rather than a 1:1:1 mapping between policy nodes, system states, and LEDs.",
      "parentUuid": "4228c774_4df161be",
      "revId": "d7ffe330ade358fe61103dc9069c0c1cfba1c7ca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
